1.Slicing in Strings
-technique use to fetch part of a string

Syntax of indexing:string[index]
Syntax of slicing:string[start:end:step]
-start:starting index at which slicing operation starts
-end:ending index at which slicing end(excluded)
-steps:integer that specifies the step for the slicing

2.Fstrings

name="john"
age=23
language="Python"
hours=3

#john is 23 years old .he studies python 3 hour a day
print(name,"is",age,"years old.He studies",language,hours,"a day")

#using-fstring
print(f"{name} is {age} years old and he studies {language} {hours} a day")

3.Escapes sequences
-\n -new line character
-\t -tab
-\\ -backlash
-\"

4.Operation on strings
*
s1="string"
print(s1*3)

#Membership
*in
s1="python"
print("p" in s1)

*not in
print("x" not in s1)

#comparison of String
print("python"=="python")
-True
print("python "=="python")
-False

#Removing spaces from string-strip()
s1="String "
print(s1.strip()=="String")
-True

#replace()-does not change original value/String
s1="we are learning Python"
print(s1.replace("Python","java"))

#to replace only one  letter
print(s1.replace("e","E",1))
print(s1.replace("n","T",3))

#count()-this count how many character/word from substring  is present in main string
#strng.count(substring)
s1="hello my name is pj from dj"
s2="j"
print(f"occurrences of j is {s1.count(s2)")

#changing cases of string
#upper()
s="Mark is a good BOY"
print(s.upper())

#lower()
print(s.lower())

#title
print(s.title())

#capitalize()
print(s.capitalize())

#startswith()-check whether the first letter of string with sub string/character
-string.startswith(substring)
